WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:09.960
Memorial Day? A national holiday to

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:13.139
celebrate those who have died in service.

00:00:13.139 --> 00:00:15.529
so thank you for those that have served

00:00:15.529 --> 00:00:17.670
and those who have passed away. Memorial Day?

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:19.230
My favorite thing about it? That's an

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.000
awkward question. Cause everybody will just

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.859
say the time off that they get on Memorial

00:00:22.859 --> 00:00:24.300
Day but reality everyone should be taking

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.699
the time to kind of think about people

00:00:26.699 --> 00:00:29.310
that have put in a lot of work and

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:32.309
sacrifice into getting us the life that

00:00:32.309 --> 00:00:33.030
we have today.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:34.380
I think Memorial Day is a good day to

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.300
think about people or grandparents

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.610
served in the military. That's kind of stuff I

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.500
think about Memorial Day. You'll find

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.420
me at the barbecue for sure. Wherever

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.489
there's a grill I will bring meat and

00:00:44.489 --> 00:00:46.110
cook on it. You know, that's my way of

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:47.789
celebrating is getting together, taking

00:00:47.789 --> 00:00:49.710
that day of relaxation and good food

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:51.449
and fellowship and hanging out. Giving thanks to

00:00:51.449 --> 00:00:55.890
those people. You know? That's what I feel. In the service. You know? To make us be able to do

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:57.539
what we get to do in life. My grandpa

00:00:57.539 --> 00:01:00.180
was in the 2nd Armored Division in World

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:02.309
War II in the European theater and then

00:01:02.309 --> 00:01:03.870
my other grandfather was stateside doing

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:05.489
maintenance and working on planes. A lot

00:01:05.489 --> 00:01:08.040
of my family's been Marine or Air Force.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.780
My grandfather was a mix, whatever that is.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:12.520
The main ship the battleship.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:15.250
Interesting story: my grandfather was

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.530
drafted in World War II after he was

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:19.690
thirty. Within a month, the law was passed

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:22.060
that no one over 30 would be drafted. My

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.190
other grandfather on the Pacific was in

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:27.250
an amphibious unit of the army. When he came

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:28.990
back after the war, he worked at a TV

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:31.300
station and then worked for the space

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:33.460
program in communications, so that's pretty cool!

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.979
Did you have any family members? Memorial Day?

00:01:35.979 --> 00:01:37.000
In World War I,

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.460
my mom's great-uncle he was a Doughboy

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:41.799
and was gassed on the front lines and he

00:01:41.799 --> 00:01:44.440
came back and he kind of lost his mental

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:46.060
capacity and, you know, dealt with all

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:48.820
sorts of diseases and then passed away. You

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:50.590
know, share the stories of those people

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:52.210
and remember them I think there's

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:54.610
honor than that you know. Enjoying

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:57.009
the freedom that they gave us? Yeah, I mean we

00:01:57.009 --> 00:01:58.360
do it every day. Look at this! You have

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:00.280
the freedom to sit around making YouTube

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:01.869
videos every day. We don't have to, like,

00:02:01.869 --> 00:02:06.250
work in mines. Gotcha. What?

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:09.600
I got you. You didn't even hear me say "Gotcha". Really? How did you get me?

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:13.050
You said the "m-word".

